    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Question\n\nAs it is, if you call for word label, you see 2 letters. You press the first letter, and then the second letter changes.\r\n\r\nfolke/flash, for example, has an option that is pretty much the same as this, but better UX, in my opinion. That is, the label remains constant. For example.\r\n\r\nIf you want to go to the word \"NeoVim\", you see the letters \"ab\" at the start. You press \"a\", and then the \"b\" letter changes to something else. On flash, it remains b, so you can be much faster.\r\n\r\nIs there already an option for this on jump2d?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.jump2d</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As it is, if you call for word label, you see 2 letters. You press the first letter, and then the second letter changes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">folke/flash, for example, has an option that is pretty much the same as this, but better UX, in my opinion. That is, the label remains constant. For example.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you want to go to the word \"NeoVim\", you see the letters \"ab\" at the start. You press \"a\", and then the \"b\" letter changes to something else. On flash, it remains b, so you can be much faster.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there already an option for this on jump2d?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.jump2d\nQuestion\nAs it is, if you call for word label, you see 2 letters. You press the first letter, and then the second letter changes.\nfolke/flash, for example, has an option that is pretty much the same as this, but better UX, in my opinion. That is, the label remains constant. For example.\nIf you want to go to the word \"NeoVim\", you see the letters \"ab\" at the start. You press \"a\", and then the \"b\" letter changes to something else. On flash, it remains b, so you can be much faster.\nIs there already an option for this on jump2d?",
