            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> If you want to go to the word \"NeoVim\", you see the letters \"ab\" at the start. You press \"a\", and then the \"b\" letter changes to something else. On flash, it remains b, so you can be much faster.\r\n\r\nCan you clarify, please? The full label sequence (as there might be more than one label needed to uniquely identify the jump spot) is computed in advance and is fixed after jumping has started.\r\n\r\nBy default only the *next label* is shown (i.e. zero steps ahead). But if you see both `ab` letters at the spot you want to jump to, then it is the whole sequence you need to type to get there. It can be adjusted it with something like [`config.view.n_steps_ahead = 2`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8ca3965e68edfee5f438d4063f5adf5afa255884/doc/mini-jump2d.txt#L185) (which is planned to be a new default after #1818).\r\n\r\nHere is the difference:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/560bbe92-686c-466d-98f5-ecf93a554682\r\n\r\nDoes this answer the question?",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you want to go to the word \"NeoVim\", you see the letters \"ab\" at the start. You press \"a\", and then the \"b\" letter changes to something else. On flash, it remains b, so you can be much faster.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Can you clarify, please? The full label sequence (as there might be more than one label needed to uniquely identify the jump spot) is computed in advance and is fixed after jumping has started.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">By default only the <em>next label</em> is shown (i.e. zero steps ahead). But if you see both <code class=\"notranslate\">ab</code> letters at the spot you want to jump to, then it is the whole sequence you need to type to get there. It can be adjusted it with something like <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8ca3965e68edfee5f438d4063f5adf5afa255884/doc/mini-jump2d.txt#L185\"><code class=\"notranslate\">config.view.n_steps_ahead = 2</code></a> (which is planned to be a new default after <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3083118846\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1818\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1818/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1818\">#1818</a>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is the difference:</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">jump2d-label-demo.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/24854248/460235739-560bbe92-686c-466d-98f5-ecf93a554682.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..K2S0gvPD3zcQ6cqyUo17wtTLWVdvIxuUNgbyWLauIWk\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/24854248/460235739-560bbe92-686c-466d-98f5-ecf93a554682.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..K2S0gvPD3zcQ6cqyUo17wtTLWVdvIxuUNgbyWLauIWk\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Does this answer the question?</p>",
            "bodyText": "If you want to go to the word \"NeoVim\", you see the letters \"ab\" at the start. You press \"a\", and then the \"b\" letter changes to something else. On flash, it remains b, so you can be much faster.\n\nCan you clarify, please? The full label sequence (as there might be more than one label needed to uniquely identify the jump spot) is computed in advance and is fixed after jumping has started.\nBy default only the next label is shown (i.e. zero steps ahead). But if you see both ab letters at the spot you want to jump to, then it is the whole sequence you need to type to get there. It can be adjusted it with something like config.view.n_steps_ahead = 2 (which is planned to be a new default after #1818).\nHere is the difference:\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    jump2d-label-demo.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nDoes this answer the question?",
